design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:13:> **NOTE 2026-07-11:** The `window.md2GithubAuth` bridge and GitHub OAuth proxy referenced below were removed with OAuth (see [[F_034_github_oauth_cors_proxy]]). GitHub auth is now PAT-only and the `connection` config section no longer exists.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:16:Provide a browsable `/config` page with sections and quick-jump tabs, typed value editors with descriptions, explicit save/cancel, and a global config service that merges values from React-app, desktop-app and project-level sources depending on the connection setup.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:19:Config is still handled by separate feature-specific paths. There is no `/config` route, no router-backed navigation, no config page UI, no draft save/cancel flow and no singleton `ConfigService`. The shared `service_injector` exists and `DataService` registers itself there, but config is passed directly into `DataService.init`.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:21:Project config is a small in-memory object. `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` builds it from hard-coded/default values: working folder `design`, default card types, default card body template and the selected push mode. `ProjectWorkspace` owns the push-mode select, recreates config when opening a GitHub or local project, and reads card types/working folder back from `DataService`. `use_app_bootstrap.ts` restores the last project with auto push mode. No project config file is loaded, merged, validated or saved.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:23:GitHub auth config is read from Vite environment values by `readGithubAuthConfig`; missing `GITHUB_CLIENT_ID` fails fast, optional proxy URL can be absent and scopes default to `repo`. Theme settings are persisted separately in `localStorage` through `useThemeSettings`, not through a general config system.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:25:Electron exposes local data, GitHub OAuth proxy and theme-mode bridges on `window.md2Data`, `window.md2GithubAuth` and `window.md2Theme`. The desktop app URL is resolved from `MD2_APP_URL` with a localhost default. There is no desktop config bridge for editable settings and no project-level config IPC/storage contract.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:27:Tests cover the current focused paths: project/session data behavior, GitHub auth config, theme settings/provider, Electron app URL resolution and desktop theme helpers. There are no config-service merge/validation tests or config-page React tests yet.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:30:- Add a singleton `ConfigService` in `app/src/services/`, registered through `service_injector`, with two-phase initialization and explicit `get`, `set`, `clear`, `loadDraft`, `saveDraft` and `discardDraft` behavior.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:31:- Define config metadata separately from values: key, section, label, description, value type, allowed options/range, default value, source (`react`, `desktop`, `project`) and editability.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:32:- Replace `createProjectConfig(pushMode)` and direct config constants with values from `ConfigService`; affected call sites are `use_app_bootstrap.ts`, `project_workspace.tsx` and `data_service.ts`. They should receive the new config behavior.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:33:- Keep GitHub env config (`github_auth_config.ts`) fail-fast for required build/runtime values, but expose editable connection settings only for values that can be changed safely at runtime.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:34:- In desktop mode, expose desktop config values through the preload bridge. Use main-process IPC only for values that require main-owned Electron APIs.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:35:- Project config is loaded after a project opens, merged over defaults, and saved through the active storage backend. Missing required project config fields fail with clear errors.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:36:- Build `/config` as a real navigable route or URL-backed view. Sections use hash anchors for quick jumps; desktop shows section tabs on the left, mobile shows them below the toolbar.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:37:- The config page edits a draft only. Save validates and applies changes to services; Cancel or leaving the page clears the draft without changing active config.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:40:- `/config` can be opened directly and navigated with browser back/forward, including section hash jumps.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:41:- Config entries are grouped by section and rendered with typed editors: switch for booleans, dropdown for known values, number input or slider for numeric ranges, and short descriptions for all entries.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:42:- Save applies validated changes to the global config service and affected services; Cancel leaves the active config unchanged.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:44:- Opening a project loads project config, merges it over defaults, and uses it for working folder, push mode and card type settings.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:45:- Invalid or missing required config shows a clear error and does not silently fall back to partial behavior.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:46:- Config draft state is created only while `/config` is open and cleared when the page closes.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:47:- Unit tests cover config merge/validation and service updates; React tests cover typed editors, save/cancel and desktop/mobile section navigation.
design\feature_descriptions\F_016_config.md:50:- `design\architecture\initial description\config.md`
design\feature_descriptions\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:18:- Add preload bridge methods to configure/test SSH connection details, list image files on the device with modified times, import selected files and persist per-device import metadata in the project.
design\feature_descriptions\F_015_remarkable_integration.md:29:- In Electron local-project mode, the user can configure/test a Remarkable SSH connection and list available image files with modified times.
